329 0 obj
<<
/A <<
/BBox [59.8677 157.946 541.026 741.154]
/O /Layout
>>
/Alt (This figure presents a multi-part overview of an experimental study on neural activity in rat brain regions related to Parkinson's disease \(PD\) and treatment effects. Panel A diagrams the basal ganglia and related brain regions, showing excitatory and inhibitory neural connections among cortex, striatum \(divided into D1 and D2 pathways\), globus pallidus external and internal segments, subthalamic nucleus, substantia nigra pars reticulata, pedunculopontine nucleus, and thalamus. Panel B outlines the experimental timeline for two groups of rats: a PD group receiving 6-&nobreak;hydroxydopamine injections into the medial forebrain bundle followed by APO testing, electrode implantation, and L-&nobreak;DOPA treatment; and a normal control group undergoing electrode implantation and recording without lesion or treatment. Panel C shows power spectral density plots of neural signals from eight brain regions \(M1 cortex, dorsal striatum, globus pallidus external, ventral anterior/ventral lateral thalamus, globus pallidus internal, subthalamic nucleus, substantia nigra pars reticulata, and pedunculopontine nucleus\) comparing PD, L-&nobreak;DOPA treated, and normal groups. The plots indicate frequency-dependent power differences across groups. Panel D provides time-frequency spectrograms of local field potentials from M1 cortex and dorsal striatum for PD, L-&nobreak;DOPA treated, and normal groups, illustrating temporal dynamics of power across frequencies up to 150 Hertz over 300 seconds. Panel E describes the data processing and analysis workflow: local field potential signals from rats in PD, L-&nobreak;DOPA treated, and normal groups undergo filtering, artifact rejection, and power spectral density extraction; these processed data feed into a hierarchical multilayer perceptron model trained with multiple loss functions and strategies to classify disease states and analyze multi-region neural activity combinations.)
/K [0 330 0 R]
/P 328 0 R
/Pg 201 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
